  </div>
  <h1>On-Policy Training for Speculative Decoding: Disaggregated Rollout-Verify-Train</h1>
  <p class="lead">
    Every speculative decoding draft model has exposure bias: it trains on clean target-generated sequences but deploys into a context contaminated by its own accepted and rejected tokens. On-policy training through the full accept/reject loop fixes this. A disaggregated Rollout-Verify-Train (RVT) architecture — borrowing prefill/decode separation from serving infrastructure — makes it scale.
  </p>
